@startuml
title Apply to a Research Opportunity — Persistent Flow
autonumber

actor Student
boundary "Opportunity Page" as UI
control "FastAPI Routes" as API
control "Application Service" as Service
database "SQLAlchemy Session" as Session
database "MySQL" as DB

Student -> UI: Open opportunity
UI -> API: GET opportunity
API -> Session: Load published opportunity and professor
Session -> DB: SELECT opportunity and professor
DB --> Session: Opportunity details
Session --> API: Opportunity and professor
API --> UI: Render details and application form
UI --> Student: Show opportunity, professor, deadline

Student -> UI: Complete form and submit
UI -> UI: Validate required application fields
alt Invalid form
  UI --> Student: Show field validation errors
else Valid form
  UI -> API: POST application with session cookie
  API -> API: Verify signed session token
  API -> Session: Load authenticated user
  Session -> DB: SELECT user by token subject
  DB --> Session: User role and profile
  Session --> API: Authenticated student
  API -> API: Verify student role
  API -> Service: submitApplication(opportunityId, student, statement)
  Service -> Session: Check opportunity and existing application
  Session -> DB: SELECT opportunity and matching application
  DB --> Session: Current records
  Session --> Service: Eligibility result
  alt Opportunity closed, expired, or duplicate
    Service --> API: Return actionable validation error
    API --> UI: Return actionable validation error
    UI --> Student: Show why application cannot be submitted
  else Eligible
    Service -> Session: Insert submitted application
    Session -> DB: INSERT application (unique student/opportunity)
    DB --> Session: Persisted application
    Session --> Service: Application ID and submitted status
    Service --> API: Submission confirmation
    API --> UI: Submission confirmation
    UI --> Student: Show success state
  end
end

note over API,DB
The signed, HttpOnly session cookie supplies the student identity;
never trust a form field for identity. The unique constraint and
eligibility checks protect persisted applications.
end note

note over Student,DB
Local prototype accounts only. Production use requires an approved
identity provider and an HTTPS deployment with secure cookies.
end note
@enduml
